 "stimulus_html": "<p>For numbers 1 – 9, use the following scenario:<br> A car has a 16-gallon fuel tank. When driven on a highway, it has a gas mileage of 30 miles per gallon. The gas mileage (also called \"fuel efficiency\") tells us the number of miles the car can travel for a particular amount of fuel (one gallon of gasoline, in this case). After filling the gas tank, the driver got on a highway and drove for a while.</p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 645909,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\">\n  <li>How many miles has the car traveled if it has 15 gallons left in the tank?</li>\n</ol>",
