  {
   "id": 645916,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"8\">\n  <li>Noah was helping to collect the entry fees at his school's football game. Student entry costs $2.75 each and adult entry costs $5.25 each. By the end of the game, Diego had collected $281.25.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Select two </strong>equations that could represent the relationship between the number of students, <span data-math=\"s\">s</span>, the number of adults, <span data-math=\"a\">a</span>, and the dollar amount collected at the game.</p>\n<ol type=\"a\">\n  <li><span data-math=\"281.25 - 5.25a=2.75s\">281.25 - 5.25a=2.75s</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"a=53.57- \\frac{2.75}{5.25}s\">a=53.57- \\frac{2.75}{5.25}s</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"x - 2 =4\">x - 2 =4</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"x - 2 = 12\">x - 2 = 12</span></li>\n  <li><span data-math=\"x -6 = 4\">x -6 = 4</span></li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [],
